From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:36:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: leave the performance selectors to
 the host governor by default

Publishing 1000 in the three Globals performance selectors, as macOS does, did not shorten
render.heavy or compute.heavy on J604 (397.5 and 595.4 us per submit at depth 64, as before)
while the GPU rail on render.heavy rose from 7.18 W to 10.5 W. Make g16_selectors=0 the
default; 1 still selects the macOS value at runtime.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index c42d279734..5656df1ac0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -1034,8 +1034,12 @@ pub(crate) fn doorbell_tally() -> bool {
     "G16: add one to the Globals doorbell tally (+0x80) before each doorbell, as macOS does (default 1; 0: never written, as before; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_selectors` (runtime 0644, default 1).
-static SELECTORS: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
+/// Storage of `g16_selectors` (runtime 0644, default 0).
+///
+/// Off by default: on J604 1.916 publishing 1000 left render.heavy and compute.heavy at the same
+/// time per submit (397.5 / 595.4 us at depth 64) while the GPU rail on render.heavy rose from
+/// 7.18 W to 10.5 W, so the same work took more energy.
+static SELECTORS: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
 
 /// Whether the three Globals performance selectors carry what macOS keeps in them (1000, the
 /// firmware chooses its state) whenever the cooling ceiling allows the top state, instead of
@@ -1050,7 +1054,7 @@ pub(crate) fn selectors_macos() -> bool {
     SELECTORS_PARM,
     SELECTORS,
     "g16_selectors",
-    "G16: performance selectors (default 1: 1000 as macOS whenever the cooling ceiling allows the top state, else that ceiling; 0: the host utilization governor's state x 100, as before; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: performance selectors (default 0: the host utilization governor's state x 100; 1: 1000 as macOS whenever the cooling ceiling allows the top state, else that ceiling; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_runtime_words` (0644, default 1; read at boot after READY).
-- 
2.43.0

